Release signing keystore for the Survival Guide app
===================================================

This is a personal, single-device app, so the keystore and its password are
deliberately committed to the repository (as requested). Anyone with this
repository can sign an update for the app. Do not reuse this key for anything else.

  File:           keystore/release.jks   (PKCS12)
  Store password: uVsfBXYuIZKPVihsvtZ7
  Key alias:      survival
  Key password:   uVsfBXYuIZKPVihsvtZ7
  Algorithm:      RSA 4096, valid 100 years
  SHA-256 cert:   74:80:DA:C3:E9:1C:14:6E:81:91:A5:DB:6A:43:83:0B:B2:D9:F5:DF:DA:3A:6C:96:E2:27:BE:B5:7B:4F:8F:69

The same values are read by app/build.gradle.kts from keystore/keystore.properties.
Keep this key: Android only installs an update (adb install -r) over the existing
app if it is signed with the same key. Losing it means uninstalling first, which
also wipes favourites/settings and (if set) requires removing device owner.
